Z||000000||Buddafingaz||04-12-2000||11:59 AM||||I was told that I would HAVE to use the orig. tranny from the LT1, because it has it's own computer ( the tranny ).  Possibly because the one's I've been inquiring about are less than 40k mis. If this IS true, how can I get by that.  Also, what kinds of things should I look out for when swapping?  All constructive comments welcomed.<p>[This message has been edited by Buddafingaz (edited 04-12-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||spiz||04-12-2000||01:53 PM||||no this is not true.<BR>i am using a 96 impala ss iron head motor, going into a 88 using izusu tranny.<BR>what you need is 93 z28 or 92 corvette computer with pass key system removed gm part# 16159278.<BR>you can use factory wiring harness but after market is esier.<BR>i am not sure yet if you will need to have a custom chip burned.||||reg||1
Z||000002||spiz||04-12-2000||02:17 PM||||i should add you can use the obdII computer if your getting the computer with the motor then use it. <BR>the obdII dosen't use a chip the computer has to be reprogramed.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||coyote||04-14-2000||08:35 AM||||you can use what ever tranny you like, if the v8 kit was put together right. also to add  the painless wiring harness is a good one, well marked and easy to use.||||reg||1
